  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Emergency WASH support for Flood Victims in Gambia</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The main objective of this $350,00 UNICEF project is to provide life-saving water, sanitation and hygiene assistance to vulnerable communities affected by flooding in Gambia. To that end, UNICEF will provide access to safe water to flood-affected households, distribute WASH kits, conduct hygiene and sanitation education in the community and in schools, and rehabilitate emergency water facilities and latrines. The project provides life-saving assistance to 42,200 people, including 10,486 women, 22,190 children, and 507 persons with disabilities.</narrative>
  </description>
